  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FSP-Flyway-UNDP-CHN-00100224</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The coastal wetlands of eastern China provide wintering, breeding, and stopover habitats for millions of migratory waterbirds of about 250 species in the East Asian-Australasian Flyway (EAAF). However, populations of globally significant waterbird species in the EAAF are declining at alarming rates. The EAAF passes through highly-populated eastern China, where rapid economic growth, incompatible use of natural resources, and ongoing population explosion have seriously impacted coastal ecosystems</narrative>
  </description>
